{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200 + multiprofile + avgpool (config_005) is the current best at 0.650 acc, and image-only (resnet50) is very weak at 0.208. The critical open question is whether combining the strong RNA signal with the weak image signal via fusion can exceed the RNA-only ceiling. This experiment (config_030: scvi_n200, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the most direct multimodal extension of the current best RNA-only configuration, using the simplest fusion (concat) and the already-characterized image encoder (resnet50). It tests the highest-level design question—does any image information add value on top of the best RNA setup?—while keeping all other hyperparameters matched to config_005 so any delta is attributable to the addition of the image modality and fusion. If it improves, it justifies further exploration of fusion type and image encoder; if it does not, it efficiently rules out a large block of multimodal configs and confirms RNA-only as the optimal architecture, saving budget for other refinements."
}

